From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Name the frozendict type object as CPython names it

Python 3.15 adds the builtin frozendict. A type used as a constant is
written in C as "Py" + the capitalized type name + "_Type", with the types
that are not spelled that way listed one by one. frozendict was not listed,
so code comparing against it referred to PyFrozendict_Type, which does not
exist; CPython's is PyFrozenDict_Type. Compiling msgspec for 3.15 stopped
with:

    module.msgspec.inspect.c: error: 'PyFrozendict_Type' undeclared
    (first use in this function); did you mean 'PyFrozenDict_Type'?
---
 nuitka/Serialization.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/nuitka/Serialization.py b/nuitka/Serialization.py
--- a/nuitka/Serialization.py
+++ b/nuitka/Serialization.py
@@ -226,6 +226,8 @@
                 return "(PyObject *)&PyEnum_Type"
             elif constant is frozenset:
                 return "(PyObject *)&PyFrozenSet_Type"
+            elif python_version >= 0x3F0 and constant is frozendict:
+                return "(PyObject *)&PyFrozenDict_Type"
             elif python_version >= 0x270 and constant is memoryview:
                 return "(PyObject *)&PyMemoryView_Type"
             elif python_version < 0x300 and constant is basestring:
-- 
